# `!between` is the negation of the inclusive `between`, so values equal to either endpoint are `false`, and nulls propagate (LANGUAGE.md §4).
mode: run
---- query
from '../../data/edge/nulls.csv'
| project id,
    val_nb = value !between (2.0 .. 4.5),
    bound_nb = id !between (2 .. 4),
    dt_nb = when !between (datetime(2024-01-02) .. datetime(2024-01-03))
| sort by id asc;
from '../../data/edge/nulls.csv'
| where value !between (2.5 .. 4.5)
| project id, value
| sort by id asc;
from '../../data/edge/nulls.csv'
| where value !between (1.5 .. 2.5)
| project id, value
| sort by id asc
---- expected
id   | val_nb | bound_nb | dt_nb
long | bool   | bool     | bool
-----+--------+----------+------
   1 | true   | true     | true
   2 | false  | false    | false
   3 | null   | false    | false
   4 | false  | false    | null
   5 | null   | true     | null

id   | value
long | real
-----+------
   1 |   1.5

id   | value
long | real
-----+------
   4 |   4.5
